Reset dbp_wasloaded in retro_unload_game so the next game re-acquires its
own automatic pad mapping.

init_dosbox() decides whether it is looking at new content with

	const bool newcontent = !dbp_wasloaded;
	if (newcontent && !reinit) dbp_auto_mapping = NULL; // re-acquire when switching content

and the acquisition itself starts with `if (dbp_auto_mapping) return;`.
dbp_wasloaded is set true once content has loaded and is never cleared again -
not by retro_unload_game(), not by retro_deinit(). That is correct for a
frontend that runs one game per process, because the flag exists to tell an
in-game reboot apart from a content switch. It is wrong for a frontend that
keeps the core loaded across games and relaunches with retro_unload_game() +
retro_load_game() - e.g. REG-Station's in-process Libra player - where every
game after the first is seen as "not new content" and silently keeps the
FIRST game's automatic mapping.

Observed on REG-Linux: launching Double Dragon and then Zeliard left the pad
mapper showing "Double Dragon" while Zeliard was running, with the pad bound
to Double Dragon's keys. Worse, it persists: the core saves the active mapping
per game, so Zeliard's own PADMAP.DBP was written out byte-identical to Double
Dragon's, and a saved custom mapping then overrides any preset the user picks -
so switching the controller type appeared to do nothing at all.

Cleared in retro_unload_game() rather than in DBP_Shutdown(), which is also
called from init_dosbox()'s own re-init path where dbp_wasloaded must survive.
Harmless under RetroArch, which closes the core between games and so starts
with the flag already false.

--- a/dosbox_pure_libretro.cpp
+++ b/dosbox_pure_libretro.cpp
@@ -3359,6 +3359,12 @@
 
 void retro_unload_game(void)
 {
+	// REG-Linux: the content is going away, so the next retro_load_game is a
+	// genuine content switch. Without this a frontend that reuses the loaded
+	// core keeps the previous game's auto-mapping (see init_dosbox's
+	// `newcontent`), and the core then saves it into the new game's
+	// PADMAP.DBP.
+	dbp_wasloaded = false;
 	DBP_Shutdown();
 }
 
